# Supabase CLI local state. `.temp` holds the linked project ref and pooler
# details; `.branches` holds local branch metadata. Neither is shared.
.branches/
.temp/

# The local stack's storage volume, if `supabase start` is ever run here.
.env

# Runtime log from `supabase functions serve`, written by nohup.
fserve.log

# 🔴 Real client data. The Sheet export is 42 records — names, email addresses,
# phone numbers and free-text descriptions — and import/02-…sql embeds the same
# payload verbatim as a dollar-quoted literal.
#
# Committing either writes 35 people's contact details into git history, where
# deleting the file does not remove them: every clone keeps the blob, and taking
# it back needs a history rewrite and a force push.
#
# The repo's convention is already this — set-profiles.sql says "do not commit"
# the real addresses, every .env is ignored, and the public form deliberately
# carries no artist emails. Client data does not get a weaker rule than that.
#
# The GENERATOR is committed. Anyone who needs the SQL re-runs it against their
# own copy of the export: `node import/build-import-sql.js`.
migrations/existing_client_data_migration.json
import/02-import-existing-requests.sql
